Answer","text":"No. Depreciation is a normal part of how replacement-cost policies pay. The questions worth checking are whether the life expectancies, ages and cap are reasonable and whether labor was depreciated."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What if I never make the repairs?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Under most replacement-cost policies you keep the ACV payment, but the held-back depreciation is usually paid only after repair or replacement within the policy’s time limit."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why does the tool ask for a cap?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Many estimates limit depreciation to a maximum percentage so that even very old items keep some value. If your estimate uses a different cap, choose it from the menu."}}],"@id":"https://ohioinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-workbench/rcv-acv-holdback-calculator/#faq"},{"@type":"WebApplication","name":"RCV/ACV Holdback Calculator","description":"RCV vs ACV calculator for property claims: list items by age and life, choose a depreciation cap and labor share, and see the check you get now.","url":"https://ohioinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-workbench/rcv-acv-holdback-calculator/","applicationCategory":"FinanceApplication","operatingSystem":"Any","browserRequirements":"Requires JavaScript","isAccessibleForFree":true,"offers":{"@type":"Offer","price":"0","priceCurrency":"USD"},"provider":{"@id":"https://ohioinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"@id":"https://ohioinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-workbench/rcv-acv-holdback-calculator/#webapplication"}]}</script>
